      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The idea may good to control better avatars before enter the event world.\n\nBut as long there is no option to add exceptions, the idea will not work very well.\n\nGood example are staff / crew / dancers / DJ who are allowed to use very red avatars for own reasons. If the channel is globally set to orange / red, then staff and dancers cannot use it too because it's global channel setting.\n\nAnd if set on very red, for staff and dancers, then it will harder to control other people to use less heavy one. The idea will not work here.\n\nMaybe make special function in Udon should added to detect your avatar ranking, then exceptions can made and the door can stay closed if you have poor ranking.\n\nBut ranking system is itself not perfect. Texture memory affects much more than a bit more polygons, because many people have GPUs with 8GB VRAM. If this VRAM get full fast, the fps will drop faster.\n\nSo yeah, if your avatar is red flagged, but only at polygon count. The rest is green or orange. The ranking system should more smarter and allow to lower ranking of avatar.\n\nNow it's purely locked on numbers. So just a bit over limit at one stat, it flagged it already red or very red as minimal because one stat. That is weird.\n\nI am not against the idea, but we need better rework on ranking system to see it more overall and not purely at one stat that is very red. And we need something to make exceptions for staff / dancers / crew members on event worlds. If we have good solution for everyone, we are all happy.\n\nThrough the time, crew has already made own black list scripts to move people out of the way in sort of prison area. And there are boards with warning not use red/very red avatars. Generally it's not allowed due ToS to block users or force change avatar, but such scripts exists to control people in event worlds. Yes, there are scripts to change you in other avatar once you enter some area.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
